  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU slave on 2-wire RS485. The manual gives baud rates 2400 to 38400 (code 2, 9600 baud, is the default), a parity/stop-bit code (default one stop bit, no parity) and a node address of 1 to 247 (default 1); 8 data bits.",
    "Input registers are read with function 04; holding registers with function 03 and written with function 16, one parameter per message. Addresses are the start addresses of the manual (30001 is address 0), so the address base is 0.",
    "Every value is a 32-bit IEEE 754 float in two registers, most significant register first (big byte order, big word order). Reads and writes must cover an even number of registers; at most 50 values (100 registers) per request. Index and code registers are also carried as floats.",
    "The Network register order holding register can switch the network port to reversed word order; this map describes the default (normal) order.",
    "Parameters marked No for the wiring system in use (3P4W, 3P3W, 1P2W) return zero.",
    "Writes to protected holding registers need the password to be entered first, and the manual says a write must be preceded by writing 0000 0005h to the write-enable registers (40513 and 40514).",
    "Left out because the manual is inconsistent: the neutral current registers (parameters 113 to 117) print a start address of 0000 that disagrees with their register numbers 30224 to 30232, and three holding registers (secondary voltage 40298, system frequency 49798, current direction connection 49832) have a hex start address that disagrees with the register number. The manual's parameter numbering has gaps (for example 23 and 26); only the parameters it prints are mapped.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
